--TEST--
`{limit, deadline}` is the only way to bound a `Core\Task` call: `timeout` is neither an option nor a member, and `race` is not a member either — `rule:concurrency/limit-and-deadline-are-the-only-bounds`, `rule:core-api/shape-rules` R2
--FILE--
<?nvs
// § 3: "The plan's `timeout(...)` is therefore not a member: a timeout on a
// group of tasks is this option". R2 makes a trailing options shape the form
// of *every* optioned member, so a wrapper function would be a second way to
// say one thing — which is what `rule:core-api/shape-rules` R20 leaves no room for.
//
// `race` is asked for the opposite reason: § 3 does not reject the idea, it
// defers it under a different spelling (`Core\Task::first`, homogeneous), so
// naming it here is what stops a `race` arriving by the back door. Both of
// the three errors below are therefore about a name that must *stay* absent.
class Bounded {
    public static function options(): void {
        var $page = Core\Task::all({rows: fn(): array<int> => [1]}, {timeout: 5s});
        echo Core\Arr::count($page->rows);
    }

    public static function members(): void {
        Core\Task::timeout({rows: fn(): array<int> => [1]});
        Core\Task::race({rows: fn(): array<int> => [1]});
    }
}

Bounded::options();
Bounded::members();
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0454]: `timeout` is not an option of this member
   --> case.nvs:13:70
%A
error[E0405]: `Core\Task` has no member named `timeout`
   --> case.nvs:18:9
%A
error[E0405]: `Core\Task` has no member named `race`
   --> case.nvs:19:9
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
